Follow-up from k228 and its review. Owner: unreagent-worker. Part of k224.

1. On the built-in defaults a missing engine is a config.Load error (unreal.editor uses ${ENGINE}), so init exits 1 with that one error and prints no preflight — in the case a new user most likely hits. Needs a lenient load in internal/config (or a preflight that runs on what could be resolved) so init still reports project, agent command, node, npm, toolkit and the rest, with the engine as the blocking finding.
2. Tests missing in cmd/launcher/init_test.go: -config never writes; a symlink (also a broken one) at the target is left untouched. Both hold today by design and in a manual run.
3. The doc comment of config.LoadIn says init uses it; only init tests do (initCommand goes through config.Load).
4. hermesEnableHint does not name init yet.
5. For the maintainer: the toolkit command printed by init hardcodes the fork URL and its ue-5.8 branch in cmd/launcher/init.go; changing it takes a release.

k246 worked, tree commit-ready (not committed). Full check green on Linux: gofmt, go vet, go test -count=1 ./..., make windows (cross-compile only; Windows behaviour unverified).

